    "verdict": "Both, and the split is per fold. On `mishra` the collapse is a threshold artifact: an unweighted OOF quantile applied to scores from a weighted model; a weighted quantile recovers 0.2328 recall there. On `moz` it is NOT a threshold artifact: recall stays 0.0000 at a realised FPR of 0.0185, so that fold is a score-scale/ranking failure. The weights are applied consistently in fitting and OOF scoring; only the quantile is unweighted, the same rule as E3/E4. Either way F3 is not a fix.",
